1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:08,216
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,686
You really thought Atoy
was Karla's brother.

7
00:00:19,769 --> 00:00:21,229
[Siony] <i>Then why did you get mad?</i>

8
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:23,440
Don't you want Atoy to be your brother?

9
00:00:23,523 --> 00:00:25,692
I wish he were, but…

10
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:28,028
you shouldn't just wish for things.

11
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:29,738
There are consequences.

12
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:32,198
I know you were hurt.

13
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:33,324
PREVIOUSLY

14
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,784
[Audrey, in English] And I'm sorry.

15
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,495
[in English] I'm sorry.

16
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:39,372
[Dmitri, in English]
<i>You seem like a good father.</i>

17
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:42,083
[in English] But I don't want you
around my daughter.

18
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,627
Why didn't you tell me?

19
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,213
Because you didn't need to know.

20
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:49,382
Dad, be honest with me.

21
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,594
You don't want Atoy for me, do you?

22
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:57,057
[in English] I'm just worried about you
and my granddaughter.

23
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,267
[Audrey] <i>Atoy is a good man.</i>

24
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:02,187
[Dmitri, in English]
<i>Everyone has a secret, child.</i>

25
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:04,105
<i>Especially someone like Atoy.</i>

26
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,857
[in English] You can't get over
that businessman,

27
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,650
because of what he did to your face, huh?

28
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:08,818
[clamoring]

29
00:01:08,902 --> 00:01:09,778
- [thumps]
- [Kurt panicking]

30
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:12,614
[in English] Alexei! What are you doing
to my brother, huh?!

31
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:15,241
[in English]
Your brother is the one who hurt me first!

32
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:17,660
[in English]
I want you to check his profile.

33
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:21,623
His name is Alexei Sokolov.

34
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:24,876
[Atoy] <i>I need Ben gone for three hours,</i>

35
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:26,878
<i>so I can do what I need to do.</i>

36
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:28,880
Is this where you get the replacement ID?

37
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,089
What's your name?

38
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:31,007
[Atoy] <i>Ben Laput.</i>

39
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:31,925
<i>Uh, Laput,</i>

40
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,885
<i>letter U, not letter O.</i>

41
00:01:33,968 --> 00:01:36,429
[device beeping]

42
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:37,847
What are you carrying here?

43
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:38,765
‪[dramatic stinging]

44
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,645
[music swells, concludes]

45
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:44,771
[beeping]

46
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:47,440
[suspicious music playing]

47
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:54,072
What's this?

48
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:57,700
[music swells]

49
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:00,036
Ground meat.

50
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,663
Do you want some?

51
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:04,124
No. Maybe that's not enough for you.

52
00:02:04,207 --> 00:02:06,501
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

53
00:02:06,584 --> 00:02:08,545
I also have three eggs here.

54
00:02:09,546 --> 00:02:10,547
Do you want them?

55
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,215
No, just go inside.

56
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,466
Okay.

57
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:16,010
Thank you.

58
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,852
[suave theme music playing]

59
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:54,465
We even drank together at the baptism of…

60
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:55,383
of-- What's this?

61
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:56,801
Why aren't we drinking now?

62
00:02:56,885 --> 00:02:59,178
Because, you know,
there's a newly opened beer house here!

63
00:02:59,262 --> 00:03:00,847
It's open at this hour.

64
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:01,764
Come with me.

65
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,308
Bro, bro, I don't know you.

66
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:04,601
- Huh?
- I don't-- don't remember you.

67
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,852
- No!
- Go home, go home!

68
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:08,354
No. Come on, bro. Just come with me.

69
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:11,733
I'll take care of you tomorrow.
I'll treat you, bro.

70
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:13,318
Come on, join me. Come on, join me here.

71
00:03:13,401 --> 00:03:15,361
- Sorry. I really don't know you.
- Huh?

72
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:16,529
Bro, come on!

73
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,740
- You know me!
- What's wrong with you!

74
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,491
Come on, bro. Come on!

75
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:21,492
[groans]

76
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:25,538
Wait.

77
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:28,708
My… My wallet.

78
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,836
My wallet-- My wallet. Give me my wallet.

79
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,463
Did you take my wallet? Where's my wallet?

80
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:35,298
I didn't take anything from you!

81
00:03:35,381 --> 00:03:37,717
- Huh?!
- I'm helping you, right?!

82
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:40,345
And you're accusing me?!

83
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,846
You're really drunk!

84
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:44,682
Atoy, make sure you double
my pay for this.

85
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,893
I'm risking my face here.

86
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:48,228
[clears throat]

87
00:03:48,311 --> 00:03:51,064
Ah-- Ah, wa-wait. My… My… My wallet.

88
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:53,650
Give me my wallet, or I'll beat you up!

89
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,610
I'll beat you up if you don't
give me my wallet!

90
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:56,611
[groans]

91
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,404
Ouch, ouch.

92
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:00,615
[panting] Atoy.

93
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:02,700
[tense music playing]

94
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,452
[Emerson] Ben. Sir Ben.

95
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,914
What's happening? B-Ben. Sir Ben.

96
00:04:07,997 --> 00:04:11,084
Wait. Hey, wake up, wake up!

97
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,335
Sir Ben!

98
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,379
Oh, no! He might be dead.

99
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:17,507
Hmm, Atoy said
only three hours, not forever.

100
00:04:17,590 --> 00:04:19,842
Sir Ben! Wake up, wake up!

101
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:25,223
[anxious music playing]

102
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:33,815
Hello, sir?

103
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:35,984
I'm already here on the rooftop.

104
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:39,112
But we have a little problem.

105
00:04:39,821 --> 00:04:41,614
I heard the security.

106
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:46,119
Looks like they're on high alert
and want to call Alexei Sokolov.

107
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,078
[Mercado on the phone] <i>That's a problem.</i>

108
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:51,457
If they see Alexei Sokolov's profile,

109
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:55,420
they'll know your identity
yesterday was fake.

110
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,880
If that happens,
the embassy will be alerted.

111
00:04:57,964 --> 00:05:02,176
They'll either lock down the embassy
or move your target.

112
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,846
And it'll be harder for us
if that happens.

113
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:09,100
Exactly! So, you need to hurry, Atoy.

114
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:11,102
[in English] Copy, sir. Ready to execute.

115
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:15,148
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

116
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:26,409
What now?

117
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:28,286
Help! Help!

118
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:29,996
[panting]

119
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:31,831
Oh no, maybe he needs mouth-to-mouth.

120
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:32,665
‪[quirky sting]

121
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:34,917
[sneaky music playing]

122
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:36,169
[mutters]

123
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,338
[whimpering]

124
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,516
[gasping]

125
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:54,145
Sir Ben. Oh, he's breathing!
Sir Ben, what happened to you?

126
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,730
Sir Ben, wake up. Wake up, wake up.

127
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:57,815
Come on. I'll help you.
What happened to you?

128
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,317
[grunts]

129
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,943
You're heavy.

130
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,237
Come here.

131
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:04,155
[grunts]

132
00:06:04,238 --> 00:06:05,656
Come here. I'll help you.

133
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,076
[groans] Come on.

134
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:08,951
Here, ride here.

135
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,620
What happened to you?

136
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:11,704
Really, what--

137
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,998
Sir Ben, did you get a heart attack?

138
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,626
[grunting]

139
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:18,503
[Emerson] Okay, hurry.

140
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:23,174
[grunts] You have to double
my pay, Atoy, okay.

141
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:25,635
Hmph! Oh, stuck. [grunts]

142
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:33,893
[suave theme music playing]

143
00:06:57,667 --> 00:07:00,670
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

144
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:08,553
[both, in Russian] Good day!

145
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:10,012
[in English] My friend, how are you?

146
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,722
[in English] Mr. Ambassador.

147
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:14,976
[in English] I would like you to meet
my lovely daughter, Audrey.

148
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,979
- Audrey, Viktor Petrov.
- Hello.

149
00:07:18,479 --> 00:07:21,524
- [in English] The ambassador of Zahran.
- [in English] Pleasure to meet you, sir.

150
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:25,403
[in English] You never told me
you had such a beautiful daughter.

151
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,780
[in English] The pleasure is mine.

152
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:31,451
[in English] And, uh, where is husband?

153
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:33,828
[in English] Oh, she is single.

154
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:35,621
[suspicious music playing]

155
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:37,582
[in English] That is impossible.

156
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:38,791
‪[Dmitri chuckles]

157
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:42,253
[in English] In that case, we have to find
somebody for you tonight.

158
00:07:42,336 --> 00:07:45,173
[in English] Um, I may not
be married, but…

159
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:47,383
I'm already taken, sir.

160
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:51,679
[in English] Well,
she may change her mind,

161
00:07:51,762 --> 00:07:55,600
depending on who
will be introduced to her.

162
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:59,437
[in English] Okay.
Let us just enjoy the party.

163
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:02,440
[in English] Do you like classical music?

164
00:08:02,523 --> 00:08:03,858
[in English] Yes.

165
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:09,155
[in English] Number one violinist
of Zahran, he is playing tonight.

166
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:12,200
[in English] That sounds wonderful, sir.

167
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:16,078
[in English] So, let us go meet my friend.

168
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,247
- [in English] Come, come with me.
- [Dmitri, in English] Thank you.

169
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,373
[indistinct]

170
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:27,298
[tense music playing]

171
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:48,319
[music fades]

172
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:51,572
- [Karla] Your food.
- Thank you.

173
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,659
Oh, Karla! Wait.

174
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:58,621
Help me here so we can finish faster.

175
00:08:59,121 --> 00:09:00,414
I don't want to, Mom.

176
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:04,043
Atoy isn't here.
He'll be home later tonight.

177
00:09:04,961 --> 00:09:08,798
[pensive music playing]

178
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:14,136
How long will you keep avoiding Atoy?

179
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,306
He might notice that you're avoiding him.

180
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:20,309
Then let him notice.

181
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,853
He'll ask questions.

182
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,315
[unsettling music playing]

183
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:28,401
I can't do what you're doing, Mom.

184
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:32,280
I can't face Brother Atoy
because I feel guilty.

185
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,490
But you didn't do anything wrong.

186
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:35,866
That's the point.

187
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:37,451
I didn't do anything wrong,

188
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:40,621
but I'm ashamed
of how you deceived his family.

189
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,083
I'm not like you, who's thick-faced.

190
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:48,337
[tense music playing]

191
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,380
[dramatic sting]

192
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:51,257
Karla.

193
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,802
Karla--

194
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:57,888
Karla.

195
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,559
[sobs]

196
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:05,354
[in English] Oh, you are going
to serve that?

197
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:06,647
[in English] Yes, sir.

198
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:08,524
[in English] No, no, no.
That is not what the ambassador likes.

199
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,776
[in English] Yes, sir.
But there's no other wine here.

200
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,695
[in English] There is in the office.
I will get it.

201
00:10:12,778 --> 00:10:13,863
Okay.

202
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:19,327
[pensive music playing]

203
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:36,302
[suspicious music playing]

204
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:50,650
[tense music playing]

205
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,458
‪[music intensifies]

206
00:11:11,754 --> 00:11:15,383
[in English] You will like
my friends, Dmitri.

207
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:17,385
[in English] It will be an honor.

208
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:21,305
[in English] Dad, I think
I'll stay behind.

209
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:23,015
I just have to call someone.

210
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:24,809
[in English] All right.

211
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,686
[in English] No. You cannot be alone.

212
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:28,854
[in English] Uh, wait.

213
00:11:29,438 --> 00:11:30,898
- Daphne.
- [Daphne, in English] Yes, sir?

214
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:33,067
[in English] Where is Samir?

215
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,860
- [in English] Look for him.
- [in English] Okay, sir.

216
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:37,488
[elegant classical music playing]

217
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:40,908
[in English] You will like
the head of my security.

218
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:45,162
[in English] He is tough, but very nice.

219
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:49,917
[in English] He's ex-military
and single too.

220
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,919
[in English] Maybe later.

221
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,255
[in English] Interesting.

222
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:56,048
[in English] Let's go?

223
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:58,634
[in English] Um, get her a drink.

224
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:02,263
[rousing music playing]

225
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:06,892
[tense music playing]

226
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,870
[line rings]

227
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:29,039
[phone ringing]

228
00:12:33,669 --> 00:12:34,670
Audrey?

229
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:35,963
[in English] Uh, hello, Atoy.

230
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:37,339
I-I just wanted to let you know

231
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:40,468
that I'm here now
at the embassy of Zahran.

232
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:43,345
What?! What are you doing at the embassy?

233
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:47,433
Um, Dad brought me to the party,
because the ambassador is his friend.

234
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:51,061
If you can, maybe don't join.
Don't go there.

235
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,229
Why?

236
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,273
Is there a problem?

237
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,400
I'm here too.

238
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:59,028
I-- I'm finishing a mission.

239
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:01,739
What? Why? What are you--
Why did you come?

240
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:03,616
What?!

241
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:05,117
Whe-- Where are you?

242
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:06,785
Whatever!

243
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,829
Where are you?!

244
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,459
- [in English] Sir Samir?
- [in English] Yes?

245
00:13:13,542 --> 00:13:14,877
[in English] The ambassador
is looking for you.

246
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:17,588
- [in English] Uh, help me.
- [Daphne, in English] Yes, sir.

247
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:19,548
[in English] Take two of this.

248
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:22,384
[tense music playing]

249
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:24,720
[in English] Look at this guy.

250
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:26,305
[in English] What a loser.

251
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:32,561
[Audrey] <i>Oh, are you here at the event?</i>

252
00:13:32,645 --> 00:13:33,938
[in English] Hello?

253
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:38,442
Hello? Why aren't you answering?

254
00:13:41,278 --> 00:13:43,572
Okay, fine. We'll talk later.

255
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:45,741
Take care.

256
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:58,796
[in Russian] You're dumb!

257
00:13:59,755 --> 00:14:04,176
[in English] Get off your phone
and get back to work!

258
00:14:05,094 --> 00:14:08,013
[tense music playing]

259
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:40,921
KARLA, WHERE ARE YOU?

260
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,007
I'VE GOT A GIG FOR YOU

261
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:46,260
SO, CAN YOU DRIVE FOR ME?

262
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:47,219
[melancholic music playing]

263
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:51,181
I DON'T KNOW WHY YOU AREN'T REPLYING TO ME

264
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,100
ARE YOU OKAY?

265
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,979
ALWAYS REMEMBER, IF YOU HAVE
A PROBLEM, YOU CAN ALWAYS COME TO ME

266
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:57,980
[phone blips]

267
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:04,445
Karla!

268
00:15:08,699 --> 00:15:11,911
- [in English] Babe, where are you going?
- To Karla.

269
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,748
But we'll be late.

270
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:18,208
This will just take a moment, okay?
I'll just check on her.

271
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:22,004
Where did she go?

272
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:27,676
Oh, she already left.
Come on, babe. Let's go.

273
00:15:35,309 --> 00:15:39,021
- [line rings, then blips]
- [knock on door]

274
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:39,980
Miss Cita.

275
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,273
Hey, Paldo, come in.

276
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:42,399
- Good day.
- Come in.

277
00:15:42,983 --> 00:15:45,611
Did you see Karla outside?

278
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,947
Uh, I ran into her earlier.

279
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:50,115
She was scowling.

280
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:53,452
I'm sure you fought again.

281
00:15:53,535 --> 00:15:55,371
Um, not really.

282
00:15:56,330 --> 00:16:01,794
Ah. My-- My friend, uh, Jeffrey,
wants to have clothes tailored.

283
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:03,003
Is Atoy here?

284
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:06,090
Oh, Atoy isn't here right now.

285
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:10,219
Is that so? I also stopped by Emerson's.
He wasn't there either.

286
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:13,681
Do the tailors have a convention today?

287
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:15,015
They're both out.

288
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:15,933
[chuckles softly]

289
00:16:16,016 --> 00:16:17,434
Probably not.

290
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:20,354
Just send him here
so I can take his measurements, okay?

291
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:22,022
What's his name again?

292
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,983
- Jeffrey. Jeffrey.
- Jeffrey.

293
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,818
Paldo, thanks for the referral.

294
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:28,153
- Of course, Miss Cita.
- All right.

295
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:32,074
[Emerson] Wait. Sir Ben.

296
00:16:32,157 --> 00:16:34,868
[pensive music playing]

297
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:36,495
Please take care of--

298
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:38,831
What happened to the patient?

299
00:16:38,914 --> 00:16:41,250
I don't, uh-- I just…

300
00:16:41,333 --> 00:16:44,586
I just saw him faint.

301
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:46,797
On the street, I just saw him faint.

302
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,216
Ah. He's not your relative?

303
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:50,968
Oh? No, no, no.

304
00:16:51,051 --> 00:16:54,763
I'm just a… I'm just a good Samaritan.

305
00:16:55,305 --> 00:16:57,307
Um, you need to sign this first.

306
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:58,225
Me?

307
00:16:58,308 --> 00:17:01,061
[heavy breathing]

308
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:03,564
I don't know. I don't know the--

309
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:05,858
Um, excuse me. Just a moment.

310
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:09,361
[heavy breathing, sharp exhale]

311
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,114
No, eh.

312
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:18,328
[line rings]

313
00:17:22,416 --> 00:17:24,001
- Hello?
- [Emerson on the phone] <i>Atoy.</i>

314
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:27,087
Uh, you need to help me here with Ben.

315
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:30,049
Looks like this guy won't be able
to return to the building.

316
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,341
Uh, I think I killed him.

317
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:33,343
[machine clangs]

318
00:17:35,012 --> 00:17:37,389
[ominous music playing]

319
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:40,601
We-- We're here now at the hospital.

320
00:17:40,684 --> 00:17:43,645
The problem is, bro, I might go to jail.

321
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:46,106
I don't want to go to jail, bro. Help me.

322
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:49,443
Hello?

323
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:50,944
[suspicious music playing]

324
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,446
Atoy, are you still alive?

325
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:54,698
Or are you just busy? Atoy!

326
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:55,657
[line beeping]

327
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:56,617
Atoy!

328
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,078
[tense music playing]

329
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:08,587
Hmm, back, length.

330
00:18:09,213 --> 00:18:10,839
- [Cita, in English] Twenty-seven.
- Yes.

331
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:13,467
[Cita, in English] Neck.

332
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:17,262
Miss Cita.

333
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:19,306
[Cita] Uh-huh? Seventeen. Oh?

334
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:20,724
Is this still working?

335
00:18:21,558 --> 00:18:23,894
It just needs a little fixing.

336
00:18:24,561 --> 00:18:25,729
[in English] Bicep, mmm.

337
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,857
Why don't you sell this?

338
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:30,943
There's a junk shop here
that will take it.

339
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:33,445
Oh, no, Atoy won't allow it.

340
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:35,656
That's Delfin's old machine.

341
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:39,034
[somber music playing]

342
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:44,456
Do you want it loose
or really fitted to the body?

343
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,666
Like this.

344
00:18:45,749 --> 00:18:47,084
Ah, okay.

345
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,502
Like this, fitted.

346
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:52,840
[Cita] Hmm…

347
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:02,724
[Cita mutters]

348
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,893
That's why this is so old school.

349
00:19:14,069 --> 00:19:17,489
Sir Delfin's death anniversary
must be near.

350
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:22,536
Oh, yes! You still remember that?

351
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:23,620
[music swells]

352
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:25,330
[car engine revving]

353
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:27,457
- [tires screeching]
- [crashes]

354
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,669
[car engine revving]

355
00:19:30,752 --> 00:19:31,795
[people panicking]

356
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:33,338
[sinister music playing]

357
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:34,631
Stupid meddler.

358
00:19:34,715 --> 00:19:36,884
Boss, that's Atoy's father, boss.

359
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:40,304
You might have killed him.
Boss, he didn't do anything wrong to us.

360
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:46,768
Sir Delfin was kind.

361
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:52,441
Everyone who knew him here in Tabang Lupa…

362
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:56,028
They all know that.

363
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:59,364
[melancholic music playing]

364
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,033
You know…

365
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,662
Sir Delfin really had an impact here.

366
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:13,962
[sighs] Just write your name
and contact number.

367
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:22,262
Do you know what Delfin said
when you were still a child?

368
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:23,597
[sighs]

369
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:25,515
He said you were a good kid,

370
00:20:26,308 --> 00:20:30,646
and he was sure
you'd grow up to be a good man.

371
00:20:37,819 --> 00:20:38,654
Really?

372
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:42,241
Mm, but then you fell in
with bad company, though.

373
00:20:42,866 --> 00:20:46,245
You've changed now, haven't you?

374
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:51,041
And if Delfin
were alive today, I'm sure…

375
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:54,294
he'd be proud of you.

376
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:57,631
[melodramatic music playing]

377
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,384
Really?

378
00:21:00,968 --> 00:21:02,386
Of course!

379
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:09,768
[phone ringing]

380
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:10,727
Hello?

381
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,108
I'll go there.

382
00:21:17,025 --> 00:21:17,859
Okay.

383
00:21:20,404 --> 00:21:23,365
Jeff, tell Benj I won't be able to join.

384
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:24,408
[pensive music playing]

385
00:21:24,491 --> 00:21:25,659
Miss Cita, I just need to run an errand.

386
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:27,035
[Cita] Okay. Take care.

387
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:27,953
All right.

388
00:21:30,330 --> 00:21:32,958
Your contact number
is already here, right?

389
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:38,046
[suspicious music playing]

390
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:01,153
[in English] To grace us
with beautiful music,

391
00:22:02,362 --> 00:22:07,951
please listen to the number one
violinist in our country, Zahran.

392
00:22:09,161 --> 00:22:11,288
[in English] This is Sasha!

393
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:13,582
[audience applauding]

394
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:16,960
[classical violing music playing]

395
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,720
[in English] Sasha is amazing.

396
00:22:27,387 --> 00:22:29,389
[in English] Number one in our country.

397
00:22:30,891 --> 00:22:32,392
[Viktor, in English]
What about you, Audrey?

398
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:35,187
[in English] Do you like
this type of music?

399
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:40,400
[in English] Yes, sir.
I like it very much. [smirks]

400
00:22:41,693 --> 00:22:45,072
[in English] Oh,
and you would like this too.

401
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:50,535
[in English] Samir,
this is my dear friend, Dmitri.

402
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:53,997
[Samir, in English]
Nice to meet you, Sir Dmitri.

403
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:58,710
[in English] And this beautiful girl
is Audrey.

404
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:04,341
[in English] This is Samir.
He is the one I've been telling you about.

405
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,469
[Samir, in English] Hello, Ms. Audrey.

406
00:23:14,184 --> 00:23:17,479
[in English] Uh, Dmitri,
come with me to my office,

407
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,981
because there is something
I want to show you.

408
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:20,899
[in English] Sure.

409
00:23:20,982 --> 00:23:21,900
[tense music playing]

410
00:23:21,983 --> 00:23:23,026
[in English] Dad.

411
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:25,862
[in English] Would you excuse us
for a moment?

412
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:32,202
Dad, please stay here.

413
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:35,122
[in English] Please, just stay here.

414
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:37,499
[music swells]

415
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:40,961
[in English] Is everything all right?

416
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:43,547
[in English] Uh, I was just telling Dad

417
00:23:43,630 --> 00:23:45,882
that I think it would be rude if we left

418
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:47,467
while Sasha is still playing.

419
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,803
[classical violin music playing]

420
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:52,931
[in English] What's really the problem?

421
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,725
Dad, I came with you here.

422
00:23:55,809 --> 00:23:58,562
And now you'll just leave me
with that man?

423
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:00,856
- [in English] You're exaggerating.
- [sighs]

424
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,316
He looks kind.

425
00:24:03,984 --> 00:24:05,193
[in English] Get to know him.

426
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:08,155
[pensive music playing]

427
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:09,281
[clears throat]

428
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:13,368
[in English] Hello, Ms. Audrey.
Shall we have a drink?

429
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:16,538
[in English] Oh, that's a good idea.

430
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:18,456
[in English] I'm getting thirsty
too, child.

431
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:22,294
[in English] Yes.

432
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:25,589
- [in English] Look. Samir, right?
- [indistinct]

433
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:28,425
[in English] Um, I'm sure
you're a great guy.

434
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:31,553
[in English] But I already have a daughter
and a boyfriend.

435
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,346
[in English] That is no problem.

436
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:36,183
[in English] But is he better than me?

437
00:24:36,892 --> 00:24:37,726
[scoffs]

438
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:41,104
[in English] Of course,
and better-looking too.

439
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:51,907
[suspicious music playing]

440
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,126
[lock clicks]

441
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:15,347
[lock clicks]

442
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:17,974
[tense music playing]

443
00:25:31,863 --> 00:25:34,866
[in English] I thought
you liked the music, Audrey.

444
00:25:34,950 --> 00:25:37,160
[in English] Why-- Why did you join us?

445
00:25:37,244 --> 00:25:38,119
[sinister music playing]

446
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:42,999
[in English] I just want to make sure
that my dad doesn't do something silly!

447
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,751
[chuckles, in English] Come on, Audrey.

448
00:25:44,834 --> 00:25:46,586
[in English] What do you think
I will do there?

449
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:48,880
[in English] Don't you trust your father?

450
00:25:48,964 --> 00:25:50,548
[chuckles]

451
00:25:50,632 --> 00:25:54,427
[in English] You have
a very protective daughter, Dmitri.

452
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:55,971
[Victor chuckles]

453
00:25:57,681 --> 00:25:58,598
[Victor, in English] Come.

454
00:25:59,557 --> 00:26:02,102
[intense music playing]

455
00:26:02,185 --> 00:26:04,729
[device blipping]

456
00:26:04,813 --> 00:26:06,106
[door lock clicks]

457
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:09,109
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

458
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:19,119
You cannot leave the group!

459
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:20,870
Who's leaving? You don't want to anymore?

460
00:26:21,454 --> 00:26:23,081
- [Red] That's fine.
- Thank you, boss.

461
00:26:23,873 --> 00:26:25,458
Boss, you let him go?

462
00:26:26,209 --> 00:26:27,794
[Red] <i>I just gave him a head start.</i>

463
00:26:27,877 --> 00:26:29,587
‪UP NEXT

464
00:26:29,671 --> 00:26:33,925
[in English] The Sokolov brothers
who attended the summit are impostors.

465
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:34,968
[in English] Are you sure?

466
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,469
[in English] I am sure, sir.

467
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:38,054
[in English] We have been compromised.

468
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:39,806
[dramatic stinging]

469
00:26:41,516 --> 00:26:43,893
- [music swells]
- [machine clangs]

470
00:26:46,604 --> 00:26:48,106
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

471
00:26:48,189 --> 00:26:50,191
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

472
00:26:50,275 --> 00:26:53,778
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

473
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:55,280
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

474
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:57,073
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
